WEBVTT

01:19.750 --> 01:23.375
[whirring, clacking]

01:23.875 --> 01:24.875
[beeping]

01:29.292 --> 01:31.125
-[water dripping]
-[beeping continues]

01:40.750 --> 01:42.167
[machine beeping]

01:50.375 --> 01:52.542
[all groaning softly]

01:52.625 --> 01:55.250
[♪ tense music playing]

02:01.750 --> 02:03.208
[groans softly]

02:11.042 --> 02:12.042
[bones crackle]

02:23.750 --> 02:27.750
[crew chattering]

02:29.833 --> 02:31.083
You gonna eat that, mate?

02:31.167 --> 02:32.333
Yeah, I was.

02:33.833 --> 02:36.208
Not supposed to have
a heavy meal before cryo.

02:36.292 --> 02:38.292
-Thank you so much.
-I'm telling you that as your doctor.

02:38.375 --> 02:40.292
-You're not a doctor.
-Yeah, well, fair enough.

02:40.375 --> 02:42.083
-[crew member laughing]
-[chattering continues]

02:44.833 --> 02:46.667
[Rahim] You all right there, gorgeous?

02:47.417 --> 02:50.542
[sighing] Honestly,
cryo really creeps me out.

02:50.625 --> 02:51.708
[Morrow] Mmm, I wonder why.

02:51.792 --> 02:54.458
That's 'cause Teng over there
with his little beady eyes,

02:54.542 --> 02:55.833
-stares at you while you sleep.
-[chuckles]

02:55.917 --> 02:58.292
[Rahim] Fucking hell.
The girl should know.

02:58.375 --> 02:59.667
[Chibuzo chuckling]

02:59.750 --> 03:02.083
-[Chibuzo] He doesn't do that. Anymore.
-[Rahim] Of course, he does. He does.

03:02.167 --> 03:03.167
[Morrow] Of course not.

03:03.250 --> 03:04.583
[Chibuzo] Morrow talked to him.
Didn't you?

03:04.667 --> 03:09.042
Mr. Teng won't be a problem unless
he wants to work 65 years for no pay.

03:09.125 --> 03:12.458
-[Rahim scoffs]
-[all] Ooh, Teng.

03:12.542 --> 03:13.542
Stingy.

03:13.625 --> 03:14.708
[Petrovitch] Teng, we love you.

03:14.792 --> 03:16.417
[Rahim] He's a nice guy.
Why you being like that?

03:16.500 --> 03:19.167
-How did you sleep?
-Good.

03:19.250 --> 03:21.958
-[Rahim] Wait. Sorry, say that again.
-[crew giggling]

03:22.042 --> 03:23.750
-[Malachite] What's that one?
-[Chibuzo chuckles]

03:23.833 --> 03:24.833
[Morrow] It's company policy.

03:24.917 --> 03:28.042
-Say that's Weyland-Yutani--
-That's us?

03:28.125 --> 03:29.625
Yeah, that's who we work for.

03:29.708 --> 03:30.750
-Oh, okay.
-Right?

03:31.458 --> 03:34.792
And they control North and South America.

03:34.875 --> 03:37.250
-And the Moon, right?
-No, that's Dynamic.

03:38.083 --> 03:39.583
Yutani has Mars and Saturn.

03:39.667 --> 03:42.542
Yeah, but we're talking about the Earth.
Who rules what.

03:43.042 --> 03:44.667
The kid hasn't done his social studies.

03:44.750 --> 03:47.750
There's four companies.
They govern the entire globe.

03:48.333 --> 03:50.458
Don't forget the new one. Prodigy.

03:51.042 --> 03:52.292
[Malachite] What's that one?

03:52.375 --> 03:57.875
Uh, it's, uh, synths, AI.
Was started by a kid maybe ten years ago?

03:57.958 --> 03:59.375
-Yeah. Boy Kavalier.
-[chuckles]

03:59.458 --> 04:01.833
-[Morrow] That's the one.
-[Petrovitch] Youngest trillionaire ever.

04:01.917 --> 04:05.417
[Shmuel]
Right. So, there's five companies, right?

04:05.500 --> 04:07.708
-[Malachite] I still don't get it.
-[Zaveri chuckles] Poor baby.

04:07.792 --> 04:08.792
[Morrow] Mr. Teng.

04:25.625 --> 04:27.750
You checked the nav computer, Mr. Teng?

04:32.042 --> 04:34.208
Are you asking if I did my job?

04:34.292 --> 04:35.875
How long to Earth's orbit?

04:35.958 --> 04:39.375
10,525,000 seconds.

04:39.875 --> 04:42.042
Plenty of… time.

04:42.125 --> 04:44.958
Months, Teng. Give it to me in months.

04:45.042 --> 04:47.167
-[Teng] Four months.
-[chuckling] Such a jerk.

04:47.250 --> 04:48.875
Give or take a few days.

04:50.000 --> 04:51.500
You all good, Captain?

04:51.583 --> 04:52.583
Hey.

04:53.375 --> 04:56.792
Comms are down.
Looks like the log files are corrupted.

04:56.875 --> 04:59.750
Well, it's probably just a glitch.
I can have a look.

04:59.833 --> 05:02.250
No. Security will investigate.

05:02.333 --> 05:04.000
We're also burning way too much fuel.

05:04.958 --> 05:08.958
I want you and Teng looking into
what system we could shut down.

05:09.042 --> 05:14.083
[Shmuel] Why don't we just,
uh, shoot Chibuzo's specimens into space

05:14.167 --> 05:16.583
and shut down her little zoo?

05:16.667 --> 05:19.042
Okay. I think he means real suggestions.

05:19.125 --> 05:21.583
[Shmuel] This is a real suggestion.
Those things give me the creeps.

05:21.667 --> 05:25.375
-[Malachite] Yeah, me too.
-The specimens are the mission.

05:27.000 --> 05:28.708
Easy for you to say, cyborg.

05:33.958 --> 05:35.750
We lost a lot of good men getting them.

05:37.792 --> 05:39.083
And for what?

05:40.250 --> 05:44.750
So the company can put shit into
our breakfast cereal to control our minds?

05:44.833 --> 05:46.667
-Okay. That is not a real thing.
-[Dinsdale chuckles] No.

05:46.750 --> 05:48.333
[Rahim] Don't know
what you're talking about, mate.

05:48.417 --> 05:51.500
The specimens are the mission. Period.

05:54.417 --> 05:58.208
Do I need to post extra security,
or restrict you to your quarters?

06:01.083 --> 06:02.167
[inhales]

06:04.208 --> 06:05.792
[♪ eerie music playing]

06:09.292 --> 06:10.292
[exhales sharply]

06:14.208 --> 06:16.083
Sullivan, Petrovitch.

06:16.167 --> 06:17.167
Got it.

06:19.875 --> 06:21.333
Wake me on final approach.

06:21.917 --> 06:22.917
[Zaveri] Will do.

06:25.750 --> 06:27.417
[Rahim] See you later, mate.

06:27.500 --> 06:28.750
[Chibuzo] Did he say minefield?

06:28.833 --> 06:30.875
[Rahim] I prefer to go back to bed,
do you know what I mean?

06:30.958 --> 06:33.958
[♪ jazz playing over speakers]

06:36.542 --> 06:39.000
[♪ performer sings in French]

06:39.083 --> 06:41.500
[performer] Thank you very much.
And hello.

06:44.167 --> 06:45.167
[metal clinks]

06:50.583 --> 06:53.583
[♪ jazz music continues]

06:57.958 --> 06:59.375
[creatures chittering]

07:04.000 --> 07:06.542
-[Malachite] You got any bedtime stories?
-[Shmuel speaks indistinctly]

07:06.625 --> 07:08.625
-[cat meowing]
-[Malachite chuckles]

07:17.667 --> 07:20.000
[creatures chittering]

07:20.083 --> 07:21.083
[creaking]

07:21.167 --> 07:22.167
[breathes sharply]

07:24.833 --> 07:29.833
[♪ jazz music continues, fades]

07:39.375 --> 07:40.875
[distorted shout]

07:40.958 --> 07:42.958
[♪ tense music playing]

07:53.500 --> 07:54.750
[distorted screams]

08:08.917 --> 08:10.000
[screeching]

08:46.750 --> 08:48.917
[birds chirping]

09:03.333 --> 09:04.333
What is it?

09:08.375 --> 09:09.417
It's a scorpion.

09:12.792 --> 09:13.875
Where did it come from?

09:15.167 --> 09:16.208
It was in the mess.

09:19.958 --> 09:21.375
What are you gonna do with it?

09:22.708 --> 09:24.458
What do you think we should do with it?

09:28.792 --> 09:29.875
Squash it,

09:30.958 --> 09:32.458
so it doesn't sting you.

09:34.125 --> 09:39.500
What if, while I'm squashing it, another
scorpion stings me to protect its friend

09:39.583 --> 09:41.625
the same way you're trying to protect me?

09:43.667 --> 09:44.708
It scares me.

09:45.375 --> 09:47.542
Think of how the scorpion must feel.

09:48.042 --> 09:49.542
Trapped under glass,

09:49.625 --> 09:51.500
menaced by giants.

09:53.542 --> 09:55.375
Okay, my darling.

09:56.458 --> 09:57.458
It's time.

10:00.292 --> 10:01.375
Do we have to?

10:03.917 --> 10:04.917
Yes.

10:06.250 --> 10:10.250
Go on. I'll be here when you wake up.

10:20.333 --> 10:21.458
Are you gonna kill it?

10:22.833 --> 10:23.917
Do you want me to?

10:31.917 --> 10:32.917
No.

10:56.792 --> 10:57.792
Is it gonna hurt?

10:58.833 --> 10:59.917
No.

11:00.583 --> 11:03.833
Told you, it's just like… falling asleep.

11:05.375 --> 11:06.375
Will I dream?

11:09.042 --> 11:12.875
I don't know. You'll have to tell me
when you wake up.

11:23.250 --> 11:25.333
[door alarm beeps]

11:28.167 --> 11:29.917
Ah, there she is.

11:31.333 --> 11:32.458
Hi.

11:32.542 --> 11:34.208
Uh, you got a little something, uh… Boop.

11:34.292 --> 11:35.292
[both chuckle]

11:36.000 --> 11:37.000
[Arthur] All right.

11:37.917 --> 11:38.958
Deep breath for me.

11:39.042 --> 11:41.500
[Marcy breathes deeply]

11:41.583 --> 11:43.167
[Arthur] There you go.

11:45.667 --> 11:47.667
[Arthur] You know, I had
the weirdest dream last night.

11:48.750 --> 11:51.375
We had a baby and it was a pig.

11:52.375 --> 11:54.625
[Dame Sylvia] Oh, wow.
I had a pig when I was a girl.

11:54.708 --> 11:57.708
It was cute. Then it was 300 pounds.

11:57.792 --> 12:01.167
[Arthur] Huh. So more of a human child
is what we want then.

12:02.958 --> 12:04.458
[Dame Sylvia] We talked about this.

12:08.083 --> 12:09.375
These are our children.

12:29.167 --> 12:30.417
[Dame Sylvia] Now focus.

12:34.667 --> 12:36.250
Is that what I'm gonna look like?

12:36.333 --> 12:38.417
Yes. That's you.

12:40.500 --> 12:43.167
-She's pretty.
-[Dame Sylvia chuckles]

12:43.875 --> 12:45.292
-[machine beeps]
-[door opens]

12:45.375 --> 12:48.667
Okay. Willkommen.

12:49.583 --> 12:51.000
Moshi moshi. [chuckles]

12:51.667 --> 12:53.167
How's our girl?

12:54.333 --> 12:56.375
-She's ready.
-[Boy Kavalier grunts]

12:57.833 --> 13:00.833
Do you know who Neil Armstrong was?

13:00.917 --> 13:02.292
He was an astronaut.

13:02.375 --> 13:04.542
Not just an astronaut.

13:05.042 --> 13:07.792
He was the first man
to set foot on the Moon.

13:08.792 --> 13:10.208
You're gonna be the first too.

13:11.500 --> 13:12.542
I'm going to the Moon?

13:12.625 --> 13:15.208
[chuckles] No… [chuckles] …silly.

13:15.792 --> 13:18.792
You're gonna be the first person
to transition from a human body

13:20.000 --> 13:21.292
to a synthetic.

13:21.875 --> 13:23.375
Because I'm special.

13:24.000 --> 13:25.042
[Boy Kavalier] That's right.

13:25.708 --> 13:29.333
You're very, very… [chuckles] …special.

13:30.750 --> 13:33.333
Do you want to see a magic trick? Yeah?

13:35.833 --> 13:38.000
[imitates wind whistling]

13:41.875 --> 13:42.875
[chuckles]

13:45.292 --> 13:48.333
[Boy Kavalier] It's pretty cool. Right?

14:00.125 --> 14:02.583
Okay, you. Up on the table.

14:04.583 --> 14:05.792
I want my brother.

14:07.750 --> 14:09.292
I told you, you can see him…

14:10.375 --> 14:11.458
when you wake up.

14:13.667 --> 14:15.500
But he can't see me.

14:16.917 --> 14:18.708
[smacks lips] No.

14:18.792 --> 14:22.458
Because it's a secret. What we're doing.

14:22.958 --> 14:24.042
Yes.

14:33.708 --> 14:34.708
Come on.

14:45.167 --> 14:46.583
Is it time to go to sleep?

14:49.917 --> 14:51.042
That's right, Marcy.

14:57.583 --> 14:58.583
Wendy.

14:59.708 --> 15:00.750
What was that?

15:06.167 --> 15:07.667
She looks like a Wendy.

15:20.917 --> 15:22.917
[machinery revs]

15:24.917 --> 15:26.333
[machine whirring]

15:45.042 --> 15:46.458
[whirring continues]

16:00.625 --> 16:04.958
[child singing]
♪ Latch on to the affirmative ♪

16:05.042 --> 16:11.458
-♪ And don't mess with Mr. In-Between ♪
-[baby babbling]

16:16.958 --> 16:18.625
[seagulls squawking]

16:30.208 --> 16:31.625
[♪ "Killer Crane" playing]

16:42.000 --> 16:44.500
♪ After the rain ♪

16:45.167 --> 16:47.625
♪ A killer crane ♪

16:48.458 --> 16:52.833
♪ After the rainbow ♪

16:52.917 --> 16:54.125
[seagulls squawking]

16:54.958 --> 17:00.333
♪ Across the sky, her graces glide ♪

17:01.625 --> 17:04.500
♪ Across the sea ♪

17:08.000 --> 17:12.625
♪ Across crea… ♪

17:12.708 --> 17:13.708
[Dame Sylvia shouting] Wendy.

17:16.875 --> 17:17.875
Wendy!

17:18.375 --> 17:19.708
We're ready for you!

17:20.542 --> 17:25.458
♪ Sunshine
I saw you through the hanging vine ♪

17:25.542 --> 17:27.583
♪ Fading away ♪

17:29.208 --> 17:30.208
Race you.

17:30.292 --> 17:33.750
♪And the sound
Steals the ground unafraid ♪

17:35.167 --> 17:37.792
-[♪ ominous music playing]
-[birds chirping]

18:10.000 --> 18:11.250
[Dame Sylvia] Wendy, darling…

18:12.542 --> 18:13.792
how are you feeling today?

18:16.083 --> 18:17.125
These are weird.

18:18.208 --> 18:19.250
Your breasts?

18:19.333 --> 18:20.417
They're weird.

18:21.833 --> 18:23.500
They move around when I run.

18:24.000 --> 18:27.792
Well, you are in an adult body now.
[chuckles]

18:29.250 --> 18:30.542
Why?

18:30.625 --> 18:32.417
Because synthetic bodies don't grow.

18:33.458 --> 18:34.625
So?

18:35.250 --> 18:39.208
How are your emotions?
You been happy? Sad?

18:39.917 --> 18:43.208
I don't know.
[whispers] They're quiet now.

18:44.583 --> 18:47.292
The human body manufactures hormones,

18:47.375 --> 18:52.250
dopamine, serotonin, estrogen,
that create moods.

18:52.333 --> 18:53.833
You don't have those anymore.

18:54.333 --> 18:55.833
We've tried to simulate them.

18:55.917 --> 19:00.000
To simulate adolescence,
as you grow into your adult body,

19:00.083 --> 19:01.958
so it's not just like flipping a switch.

19:02.500 --> 19:06.292
But maybe
we need to increase the intensity.

19:09.042 --> 19:12.500
We've had this discussion.
She's not human anymore.

19:12.583 --> 19:14.208
Why are we pretending she is?

19:14.917 --> 19:17.708
"She" is sitting right there,

19:18.250 --> 19:21.667
and it's the protocol
as laid out by the CEO.

19:22.208 --> 19:24.458
The body is a vessel for the mind.

19:24.542 --> 19:28.667
A human mind, on its path to endless life.

19:29.208 --> 19:31.583
Simulating the human experience
is critical.

19:33.250 --> 19:34.708
So, what am I?

19:36.833 --> 19:38.167
If I'm not human,

19:39.417 --> 19:40.667
what am I?

19:42.583 --> 19:44.125
Whatever you want to be.

19:46.208 --> 19:49.042
[Dame Sylvia] I got you something,
for your collection.

19:52.042 --> 19:54.167
Oh, and I have good news.

19:55.875 --> 19:57.417
The other children have arrived.

20:00.042 --> 20:01.167
I'm not alone anymore?

20:01.250 --> 20:04.917
Darling, you're never alone. You got us.

20:07.375 --> 20:09.333
But yes, now, there will be others.

20:09.417 --> 20:10.458
Like me?

20:10.542 --> 20:11.542
Not yet.

20:12.625 --> 20:13.958
They're still children.

20:14.917 --> 20:17.875
So we need to help them to make
the transition, so they're not afraid.

20:20.458 --> 20:21.625
Can you do that?

20:23.750 --> 20:25.042
Can you be a big sister?

20:33.292 --> 20:35.167
[Wendy] Listen now. Hear up!

20:35.250 --> 20:37.292
You can grow big and strong like me.

20:41.500 --> 20:42.833
Who wants a ride?

20:42.917 --> 20:44.917
[all] Me! Me! Me! Me! Me! Me!

20:45.000 --> 20:46.875
-[Wendy laughs]
-[chuckles]

20:46.958 --> 20:49.167
-Whoa.
-[children laughing]

21:03.083 --> 21:05.042
[Wendy] And you'll be super fast too.

21:06.667 --> 21:08.833
Were you sick too? Before.

21:10.542 --> 21:13.583
Dying even. And everybody was so sad.

21:15.917 --> 21:17.792
But then the boy genius came along,

21:18.625 --> 21:20.000
and he said… [finger snaps]

21:20.708 --> 21:23.708
"Don't be sad.
I'm gonna fix you right up."

21:25.208 --> 21:26.833
And that's exactly what he did.

21:28.167 --> 21:29.833
He gave me this big girl body.

21:30.583 --> 21:31.792
Better than new.

21:33.208 --> 21:34.500
Now I'm the forever girl.

21:35.000 --> 21:38.625
[Child Slightly]
Because grown-up minds don't fit?

21:39.125 --> 21:41.417
Uh, because grown-up minds are too stiff,

21:42.083 --> 21:43.583
so they can't make the trip yet,

21:44.083 --> 21:47.083
but our minds, kid minds,
we fit just right.

21:48.375 --> 21:49.375
Question?

21:49.875 --> 21:51.500
Will I be able to walk again?

21:52.500 --> 21:55.625
You'll be able to walk,
run, jump, dance. [chuckles]

21:56.542 --> 21:58.750
-[Wendy] Do you guys like to dance?
-[all] Yeah.

22:01.292 --> 22:04.208
-Question?
-I want to be a scientist when I grow up.

22:04.292 --> 22:06.750
Okay. That's not a question,

22:07.917 --> 22:08.917
but cool.

22:10.000 --> 22:11.292
[Wendy chuckles]

22:11.375 --> 22:13.083
When do we get to go home?

22:17.208 --> 22:18.208
You don't.

22:19.625 --> 22:20.625
[chuckles]

22:33.125 --> 22:34.667
I'll be here the whole time, okay?

22:35.875 --> 22:36.875
Promise?

22:37.875 --> 22:38.875
Promise.

22:40.542 --> 22:42.083
Uh, can you move, please? I need to begin.

22:42.167 --> 22:43.167
Go around.

22:47.583 --> 22:49.000
You want to see a magic trick?

22:51.292 --> 22:52.833
Yeah.

22:52.917 --> 22:54.542
[machine whirring]

22:54.625 --> 22:56.125
[♪ dramatic music playing]

23:21.917 --> 23:23.333
[whirring continues]

24:03.208 --> 24:05.042
[Boy Kavalier] "Mrs. Darling
first heard of Peter

24:05.875 --> 24:08.667
when she was tidying up
her children's minds.

24:09.167 --> 24:11.875
It is the nightly custom
of every good mother,

24:12.375 --> 24:14.167
after her children are asleep,

24:14.250 --> 24:17.292
to rummage in their minds
and put things straight.

24:18.875 --> 24:20.292
When you wake in the morning,

24:21.083 --> 24:23.875
the naughtinesses and evil passions
with which you went to bed,

24:24.458 --> 24:27.792
have been folded up small
and placed at the bottom of your mind.

24:28.667 --> 24:34.000
And on the top, beautifully aired,
are spread out your prettier thoughts,

24:34.500 --> 24:35.542
ready for you to put on.

24:37.042 --> 24:38.375
In the old days,

24:38.458 --> 24:39.458
at home,

24:39.958 --> 24:44.875
the Neverland had always begun to look
a little dark and threatening by bedtime.

24:46.375 --> 24:49.667
Then unexplored patches arose in it
and spread.

24:51.000 --> 24:53.458
Black shadows moved about in them.

24:54.708 --> 24:59.667
The roar of the beasts of prey
was quite different now, and above all,

25:00.583 --> 25:03.500
you lost the certainty
that you would win."

25:03.583 --> 25:05.417
[♪ dramatic music continues]

25:42.167 --> 25:43.250
[alarm blaring]

25:48.583 --> 25:51.875
-[clattering]
-[cat growling]

25:54.250 --> 25:55.500
[Mother] Collision imminent.

25:56.667 --> 25:58.208
-[distorted screaming]
-[Mother] Collision imminent.

26:03.917 --> 26:04.917
[beeping]

26:11.167 --> 26:13.167
[beeping continues]

26:18.958 --> 26:22.125
[alarm blaring]

26:22.208 --> 26:23.458
-[alarm stops]
-[beeping]

26:32.125 --> 26:33.250
Morrow!

26:34.625 --> 26:36.250
[muffled] Morrow! Let me in!

26:37.458 --> 26:39.833
Please! It's coming.

26:39.917 --> 26:41.375
-[alarm blaring]
-Let me in!

26:41.458 --> 26:42.458
[alarm stops]

26:45.083 --> 26:46.583
[muffled] Morrow, let me in!

26:50.083 --> 26:52.292
-[alarm blaring]
-What are you doing? Let me in!

26:52.375 --> 26:53.708
[muffled] It's coming.

27:01.792 --> 27:04.417
Hurry. Hurry up. It's coming.

27:07.375 --> 27:10.375
No. What are you doing?
No, no, no. Let me in!

27:10.458 --> 27:13.167
Morrow! Oh, no!

27:13.250 --> 27:15.083
Why are you doing this?

27:15.750 --> 27:17.333
You fucking asshole!

27:20.792 --> 27:22.917
[Morrow humming]

27:28.333 --> 27:29.958
-[humming continues]
-[Zaveri crying] No.

27:30.042 --> 27:31.750
[Zaveri] No!

27:33.167 --> 27:34.417
[grunting]

27:35.000 --> 27:38.000
-[creature screeching]
-[Zaveri screaming]

27:40.667 --> 27:42.250
-[Morrow humming]
-[thudding]

27:42.333 --> 27:44.667
-[creature chattering]
-[Zaveri groaning]

28:04.250 --> 28:06.375
[hisses, growls]

28:15.208 --> 28:16.375
[screeches]

28:20.667 --> 28:22.500
[screeching]

28:24.917 --> 28:25.917
[metal rattling]

28:30.708 --> 28:32.958
Mother, I need the impact room.

28:40.958 --> 28:42.208
[screeching]

28:44.375 --> 28:46.625
[Mother] Collision imminent.

28:46.708 --> 28:48.750
-[screeching]
-[Mother] Collision imminent.

28:48.833 --> 28:49.833
-[Morrow humming]
-[banging]

28:49.917 --> 28:53.583
-[Mother] Collision imminent.
-[squealing]

28:53.667 --> 28:55.792
-[humming continues]
-[machine whirring]

28:55.875 --> 28:57.375
[Mother] Collision imminent.

28:58.458 --> 29:00.542
[Mother] Collision imminent.

29:00.625 --> 29:03.208
[Mother] Collision imminent.

29:03.292 --> 29:07.708
-[squealing continues]
-[Mother] Impact in T-minus ten seconds.

29:08.542 --> 29:09.833
[Mother] Nine…

29:14.208 --> 29:17.167
[Mother] …four, three, two…

29:21.083 --> 29:22.583
[alarm blares]

29:44.458 --> 29:46.292
[train horn blaring]

29:51.667 --> 29:53.417
[motorcycle revving]

29:57.875 --> 30:02.333
[commentator 1 speaking indistinctly]

30:02.417 --> 30:03.792
[commentator 2] Yeah,
like you were saying.

30:03.875 --> 30:06.333
Easy pop-up to center field.
That's two down.

30:06.417 --> 30:08.042
[♪ rap music playing]

30:14.417 --> 30:15.417
[exhales sharply]

30:19.083 --> 30:20.667
[Wendy] Well, I'm glad you asked.

30:21.208 --> 30:22.208
See ya.

30:22.292 --> 30:23.292
[Wendy] His name is Joe.

30:24.958 --> 30:27.083
Joe DiMaggio, like the baseball player.

30:27.167 --> 30:29.583
[commentator 2] Counts two and two
and we're in third. Ready to break.

30:29.667 --> 30:30.750
[baseball bat cracks]

30:30.833 --> 30:32.458
[commentator 2]
Oh, Wilson got a hold of it.

30:32.542 --> 30:36.000
It's got the height,
and it's got the distance.

30:36.083 --> 30:37.417
Two-run homer for Wilson.

30:37.500 --> 30:40.292
-[Joe] Yes!
-And… take the lead. Two to nothing.

30:41.958 --> 30:43.083
[Wendy] What does he do?

30:44.833 --> 30:46.583
Well, he's a medic.

30:47.083 --> 30:48.167
Like a doctor.

30:50.000 --> 30:51.000
Hello.

30:51.083 --> 30:52.667
Dad used to always say that.

30:54.792 --> 30:55.958
Where are you going?

30:57.000 --> 30:58.125
Medic's pretty cool.

30:58.208 --> 30:59.208
[chuckles]

31:01.333 --> 31:02.583
He's really good at it too.

31:19.833 --> 31:20.833
She…

31:22.583 --> 31:24.083
She's watching the brother again.

31:26.958 --> 31:28.333
[Wendy] Who does he work for?

31:32.500 --> 31:33.667
He works for Prodigy.

31:35.000 --> 31:36.000
Just like us.

31:38.208 --> 31:41.375
He has to work with soldiers,
who work with guns.

31:44.083 --> 31:45.292
They told him I died.

31:51.292 --> 31:52.292
[chattering]

32:06.583 --> 32:09.708
[both speaking Thai]

32:13.375 --> 32:14.542
[Wendy] What's for dinner?

32:15.417 --> 32:16.875
I miss eating.

32:18.333 --> 32:19.958
[baseball commentary continues]

32:22.542 --> 32:24.417
[exhales sharply] There you are.

32:36.208 --> 32:39.417
[Diego] Am I hallucinating,
or is that ice coming straight towards us?

32:39.500 --> 32:42.583
[Manny] Yeah, yeah, it's coming.
It sounds like there's animals on it.

32:42.667 --> 32:46.083
[Sid] Yippee! We're being rescued!
We're being rescued!

32:46.167 --> 32:47.458
[Diego] I hear laughter.

32:48.250 --> 32:49.708
[Sid] Must be a party cruise.

32:51.542 --> 32:52.833
[Captain Gutt] Ahoy, down there!

32:53.625 --> 32:56.708
You know, these waters
are infested with pirates.

32:59.375 --> 33:02.000
-Captain Gutt here to help!
-[chuckles]

33:02.792 --> 33:04.500
[Manny] Look, we don't want any trouble.

33:04.583 --> 33:07.917
-Now surrender your ship or face my…
-Surrender your ship or face my…

33:08.000 --> 33:09.333
-…fury.
-…fury.

33:09.417 --> 33:10.875
-Or face your furry what?
-Or face your furry what?

33:10.958 --> 33:13.542
-[Captain Gutt] Not "furry." Fury!
-Fury. [chuckles]

33:13.625 --> 33:14.792
[Captain Gutt] Fire!

33:18.208 --> 33:19.250
Good night, Joe.

33:40.333 --> 33:41.417
Let's go.

33:42.125 --> 33:45.333
[Rashidi] Now? Really? [sighs]

33:49.042 --> 33:51.875
Hey, uh, what did the robot say yesterday?

33:52.583 --> 33:54.458
I gotta serve out my contract.

33:55.208 --> 33:56.208
Right.

33:57.917 --> 33:59.042
-[grunts]
-Come on.

33:59.125 --> 34:00.542
[Rashidi] Hey, eyes on the ball, Brahma.

34:00.625 --> 34:02.583
[metal rattling]

34:05.417 --> 34:06.583
What about medical school?

34:08.667 --> 34:10.208
So we're stuck with you.

34:12.417 --> 34:15.042
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

34:17.000 --> 34:19.000
-You love me.
-Babe.

34:19.583 --> 34:21.750
-[exhales sharply]
-You're just afraid to say the words.

34:25.000 --> 34:26.292
[Rashidi] Holy shit!

34:40.083 --> 34:42.042
-[Siberian] What the fuck?
-Call it in.

34:42.125 --> 34:43.875
-Captain…
-Call it in!

34:43.958 --> 34:44.958
-[clamoring]
-Everyone okay?

34:45.042 --> 34:48.458
[Siberian] This is Sigma-Prime. We have
a downed spacecraft, multiple casualties.

34:48.542 --> 34:49.750
We're heading to the crash site.

35:00.167 --> 35:01.875
[horn honking]

35:14.917 --> 35:17.458
[indistinct radio chatter]

35:17.542 --> 35:19.292
All right, by the book.

35:19.375 --> 35:23.042
Locate the survivors,
evacuate the wounded, secure the site.

35:23.125 --> 35:24.250
[all] Yes, sir!

35:24.833 --> 35:26.458
[siren wailing]

35:34.083 --> 35:36.625
[tires screeching]

35:36.708 --> 35:38.667
-[air brakes hissing]
-[siren blaring]

35:39.417 --> 35:41.125
-[Nagg] Members, check your weapons.
-[all] Yes, sir.

35:41.208 --> 35:42.292
Check.

35:42.375 --> 35:44.917
[Nagg] Brahma, upstairs.
Prep to evac the wounded.

35:45.000 --> 35:46.000
[Brahma] Yes, sir.

35:46.083 --> 35:48.083
-Rashidi, take four to the ground floor.
-Yes, sir.

35:48.167 --> 35:50.708
[Nagg] We're moving!
Go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go!

35:50.792 --> 35:54.208
Go, go, go, go! Move, move, move!

35:54.292 --> 35:55.792
Let's search for the wounded now!

35:55.875 --> 35:57.583
-[people clamoring]
-[Nagg] Two by two!

35:57.667 --> 35:59.792
Come on then! Come on then!
[echoing] Come on now!

36:00.333 --> 36:02.458
-[distorted echoes]
-[siren wailing]

36:07.708 --> 36:08.708
[Nagg] There we go!

36:09.208 --> 36:11.083
Bring it down! Bring it down!

36:13.375 --> 36:15.958
-[civilian 1] Help! Help! Help!
-[people clamoring]

36:31.000 --> 36:32.125
[metal creaking]

36:32.208 --> 36:35.375
[Rashidi] Keep moving, keep moving!
Hermit, with me, with me, let's go!

36:38.875 --> 36:42.250
-Medic tent to the right!
-Keep going!

36:42.333 --> 36:45.125
If you're hurt, head to the medics!
There's more medics coming!

36:45.875 --> 36:47.750
-[Rashidi] Keep moving!
-[clamoring continues]

36:49.083 --> 36:51.250
-[officer 1] Go! Go! Go!
-[officer 2] Get inside!

36:51.333 --> 36:52.375
[siren wailing]

36:55.583 --> 36:58.500
[Nagg] Move! Move! Move! Go! Go! Go!

37:01.833 --> 37:02.833
Let's move it, people!

37:02.917 --> 37:05.500
-Two that way, three that way.
-Yes, sir.

37:05.583 --> 37:06.792
Follow me.

37:06.875 --> 37:08.792
[announcer through PA system]

37:08.875 --> 37:10.167
[Hermit] Anybody injured?

37:10.250 --> 37:12.250
[Rashidi] Security services!

37:12.333 --> 37:15.000
-[Hermit] Anybody hurt?
-[Rashidi] Search and rescue!

37:16.542 --> 37:17.792
[Siberian] Search and rescue!

37:19.708 --> 37:21.458
[Rashidi] Search and rescue! Moving in!

37:22.833 --> 37:24.333
[Hermit] Search and rescue!

37:26.833 --> 37:28.917
-[Hermit] Search and rescue!
-[Rashidi] Hermit!

37:31.000 --> 37:32.542
-[Hermit] Got it.
-[Rashidi] Yeah.

37:32.625 --> 37:33.917
[Siberian] Search and rescue!

37:34.000 --> 37:35.292
[Rashidi] Search and rescue!

37:37.875 --> 37:39.167
Keep up.

37:42.458 --> 37:43.875
[announcer through PA system continues]

37:45.250 --> 37:46.625
[Rashidi] Ears on.

37:48.000 --> 37:49.458
I've got voices down here.

37:58.375 --> 37:59.708
[Rashidi] Security services!

37:59.792 --> 38:01.083
-You good?
-[Siberian] Yes.

38:01.167 --> 38:02.792
[Rashidi] Search and rescue.

38:02.875 --> 38:04.333
[Siberian] Search and rescue!

38:05.208 --> 38:06.958
-[Hermit] Anybody hurt?
-[Siberian] Search and rescue!

38:07.042 --> 38:08.208
-[baby crying]
-[person shrieks]

38:10.167 --> 38:11.667
[barking]

38:11.750 --> 38:12.750
Control the dog, man.

38:12.833 --> 38:14.750
-[Hermit] Search and rescue!
-[Rashidi] Coming in!

38:14.833 --> 38:16.625
-[Rashidi] Coming in!
-[Siberian] Cap.

38:16.708 --> 38:17.958
[Rashidi] Hermit! You all right?

38:18.042 --> 38:19.542
-Please evacuate the building.
-Coming in.

38:19.625 --> 38:21.292
-Use the medical center outside.
-Hermit!

38:21.375 --> 38:22.958
-[Hermit] Sir, can you hear me?
-[Siberian] We got medical.

38:23.042 --> 38:25.125
-Hey, Anant, give some blood to Hermit.
-[Anant] Got it.

38:26.042 --> 38:27.542
-You all right, Hermit?
-Yes.

38:27.625 --> 38:29.500
-[Siberian] Search and rescue!
-[Rashidi] Search and rescue!

38:29.583 --> 38:31.042
-[Cortez] Is he gone?
-[Rashidi] Hermit?

38:31.125 --> 38:32.333
[Hermit] Holy shit.

38:32.417 --> 38:34.042
[electricity crackling]

38:48.417 --> 38:50.208
[Rashidi] Looks like she goes
all the way down.

38:50.292 --> 38:51.458
-[Rashidi] Cortez.
-Yes, sir.

38:51.542 --> 38:54.042
-Radio for a fire suppression unit.
-[Cortez] Got it, Cap.

38:54.125 --> 38:56.625
[Rashidi] Anybody smells sulfur,
call it out.

38:56.708 --> 38:58.417
-[Rashidi] Let's move in.
-[Siberian] Roger.

38:58.500 --> 39:00.125
-This is Cortez to dispatch.
-[radio chattering]

39:00.208 --> 39:03.917
We have a 10-50 F situation.
I repeat, we have a 10-50 F situation.

39:04.000 --> 39:05.000
[indistinct radio chatter]

39:05.083 --> 39:07.083
[♪ tense music playing]

39:09.375 --> 39:12.000
[Cortez] We got multiple injuries,
a death, and property damage.

39:12.083 --> 39:13.292
Requesting for an ambulance…

39:18.042 --> 39:19.042
[Siberian] Search and rescue!

39:22.042 --> 39:23.208
Good luck, guys.

39:24.875 --> 39:25.875
Fucking hell.

39:25.958 --> 39:26.958
Come on.

39:27.917 --> 39:29.458
Look at the size of that thing.

39:29.542 --> 39:32.583
-I should have called in sick.
-[chuckles]

39:33.083 --> 39:36.250
Well, don't worry,
I brought spare panties in my pack.

39:36.333 --> 39:37.333
[chuckles]

39:39.167 --> 39:40.833
[Hoyt coughs]

39:48.375 --> 39:49.667
Come on.

39:58.083 --> 39:59.458
What kind of ship is this?

39:59.958 --> 40:02.667
Science vessel, I think.
It's Weyland-Yutani.

40:03.458 --> 40:05.292
I used to collect the cards
when I was a kid.

40:05.917 --> 40:07.125
Think there's a finder's fee?

40:07.208 --> 40:08.417
Lock that shit down.

40:09.250 --> 40:10.750
[hissing]

40:11.667 --> 40:13.167
Hoyt, Anant.

40:14.000 --> 40:15.417
-Copy that.
-Let's move.

40:15.500 --> 40:16.833
Let's move. With me.

40:40.208 --> 40:41.458
[electrical humming]

40:45.542 --> 40:46.750
[electricity crackling]

41:11.417 --> 41:13.167
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

41:16.250 --> 41:18.500
[breathing heavily]

41:26.500 --> 41:28.583
-[TV continues, indistinct]
-[electricity crackling]

41:41.000 --> 41:42.083
[hissing]

41:52.583 --> 41:55.625
Mother, this is Morrow. Alert Weyland HQ.

41:55.708 --> 41:59.167
The ship has been boarded.
Status of cargo unknown.

42:00.375 --> 42:04.250
I'm moving to the armory and will secure
the site until reinforcements can arrive.

42:11.583 --> 42:12.667
[Wendy humming]

42:14.042 --> 42:15.333
All right.

42:16.042 --> 42:17.458
I need you to put these on.

42:20.375 --> 42:22.875
And when you hear a tone, raise your hand.

42:22.958 --> 42:25.083
-Okay. [chuckles]
-Okay. [chuckles]

42:30.750 --> 42:32.083
Why don't you have kids?

42:34.292 --> 42:38.458
Well, we t… we tried to have kids,
but I… I have a low sperm count.

42:38.542 --> 42:41.542
-Sperm. [chuckles]
-Yeah, sperm. It's a funny word.

42:42.042 --> 42:46.583
Isn't a sperm what comes out of a boy
and then goes into the girl's egg?

42:47.375 --> 42:48.542
Yes, that's right.

42:49.292 --> 42:50.542
Yeah.

42:50.625 --> 42:53.458
[technician 1] She's beyond
all human frequencies, 75,000 Hz.

43:04.625 --> 43:05.917
Oh, Wendy, we're, uh…

43:06.000 --> 43:08.417
Put these back on,
we're not… we're finished yet.

43:15.750 --> 43:17.750
-[technician 1] What's she--
-[Arthur] Shh!

43:19.833 --> 43:21.667
[people screaming and clamoring]

43:24.458 --> 43:25.458
[breathes shakily]

43:25.542 --> 43:27.708
[Atom Eins] The ship touched down
at 17:30.

43:27.792 --> 43:30.750
It's a deep space
research vessel, C class.

43:32.208 --> 43:33.625
Weyland-Yutani.

43:33.708 --> 43:35.083
Survivors?

43:35.167 --> 43:37.625
On the ship? Unknown. Comms are down.

43:37.708 --> 43:39.375
The ship must have clipped the tower.

43:40.208 --> 43:41.958
But we have forces on the ground.

43:42.542 --> 43:45.625
Mass casualties, I'd imagine,
among the residents.

43:46.167 --> 43:48.333
Luckily, it was
the Founder's Day festival.

43:48.958 --> 43:51.125
-Hundreds of people were at the park.
-[Boy Kavalier] Mmm.

43:51.208 --> 43:52.458
-Sir--
-Not now.

43:52.542 --> 43:54.083
-Let's go.
-Uh, no. No.

43:54.167 --> 43:56.667
[Boy Kavalier] Triage the rescue
by income bracket. Call up the reserves,

43:56.750 --> 43:59.417
and keep this quiet
until we know the damage.

43:59.917 --> 44:00.917
We can do it.

44:01.000 --> 44:02.000
And the ship?

44:02.667 --> 44:06.375
Ooh, uh, a deep space research vessel
loaded with who knows what?

44:06.458 --> 44:07.625
I think that's ours now.

44:07.708 --> 44:09.167
She won't like that.

44:09.708 --> 44:12.333
-Yutani.
-Yeah, so she can sue.

44:12.417 --> 44:14.167
I said we can do it.

44:17.417 --> 44:20.208
Sir, we're fast, we're strong,
we don't break.

44:21.250 --> 44:23.875
You made us. We can do it.

44:25.167 --> 44:26.625
Rescue people, clean up.

44:29.458 --> 44:30.667
Why?

44:30.750 --> 44:35.000
The brother from her old life,
he's a medic with the tactical unit.

44:35.083 --> 44:36.708
They're inside the tower.

44:39.125 --> 44:40.583
[Boy Kavalier] So you want to help him?

44:42.208 --> 44:43.792
Look at her face.

44:44.542 --> 44:45.542
Her body language.

44:45.625 --> 44:48.042
I mean, if I didn't know better,
I'd say she was human.

44:49.708 --> 44:51.042
I am human.

45:02.167 --> 45:03.167
[chuckles]

45:07.375 --> 45:08.708
Send them.

45:09.375 --> 45:11.792
-Send…
-[Boy Kavalier] Yeah, the Lost Boys.

45:12.292 --> 45:14.042
Let's see how they handle the stress.

45:14.125 --> 45:16.000
I want all technicians on deck.

45:16.083 --> 45:17.750
Monitor brain function,
emotional response,

45:17.833 --> 45:19.417
see how the enhanced physiognomy performs.

45:19.500 --> 45:21.625
Sir, they're not first responders.

45:22.458 --> 45:24.333
They're still in the prototype stage,

45:24.417 --> 45:26.458
the loss of a single unit
will be devastating.

45:26.542 --> 45:28.208
Yeah, yeah. So don't lose one.

45:29.000 --> 45:30.333
You'll watch them?

45:31.583 --> 45:33.333
And they can follow orders, I mean…

45:34.208 --> 45:38.125
You can follow orders, right?

45:39.792 --> 45:41.125
Sir, yes, sir.

45:45.458 --> 45:46.833
See?

45:48.583 --> 45:49.667
Off you pop.

45:54.042 --> 45:56.042
[♪ dramatic music playing]

45:57.375 --> 45:58.375
[chuckles]

46:12.292 --> 46:13.917
I was sick before we got sick.

46:14.000 --> 46:16.042
Like, always sick, kind of.

46:16.125 --> 46:17.708
"No immune system," my mum said.

46:18.250 --> 46:19.250
Not me.

46:20.042 --> 46:22.833
Healthy as a horse. [imitates gunfire]

46:23.333 --> 46:26.333
Why a horse? Are they extremely healthy?

46:26.417 --> 46:31.000
Hmm. Anything is only ever as healthy
as it is, 100% being the healthiest.

46:31.500 --> 46:32.708
I didn't like it.

46:34.292 --> 46:35.292
Being sick.

46:35.792 --> 46:38.208
-[scoffs] Nobody likes it.
-[Nibs laughs]

46:38.292 --> 46:39.292
No.

46:40.708 --> 46:41.917
It was scary.

46:43.875 --> 46:46.375
Lying in my bed every night
thinking I could die.

46:47.417 --> 46:48.417
[Slightly] Now we can't die.

46:48.500 --> 46:50.833
We can still be crushed or, like,
explode though.

46:50.917 --> 46:52.875
Or be set on fire. Wait, could we drown?

46:52.958 --> 46:56.042
Yeah, like a hippo could come
and maul us or a crocodile--

46:56.125 --> 46:58.292
But not grow old or get cancer.

47:00.333 --> 47:01.333
Right?

47:05.583 --> 47:09.625
Maybe our batteries
just run out and we're, like…

47:09.708 --> 47:11.292
[imitates machine powering down]

47:12.375 --> 47:14.167
-[blows raspberry]
-[all laughing]

47:14.875 --> 47:17.000
[Wendy] Standing, dressing, running.

47:17.083 --> 47:21.125
We got a life-or-death
spaceship crash rescue mission.

47:23.583 --> 47:24.750
Seriously?

47:25.667 --> 47:27.667
[♪ tense music playing]

48:04.208 --> 48:05.208
[electricity crackling]

48:11.000 --> 48:12.125
[electronic screeching]

48:20.167 --> 48:21.333
[crackling continues]

48:21.417 --> 48:24.667
[Hoyt] Search and rescue! Is anyone here?

48:54.667 --> 48:56.333
[electronic screeching]

49:04.333 --> 49:05.542
You first.

49:05.625 --> 49:06.708
[sighs]

49:06.792 --> 49:07.792
Of course.

49:21.333 --> 49:22.542
Oh, fuck!

49:23.208 --> 49:24.250
[Hoyt] Oh, man.

49:42.875 --> 49:45.333
What the hell is that?

49:50.917 --> 49:51.917
[gasps, exhales sharply]

49:53.625 --> 49:54.625
[chuckles]

49:55.667 --> 49:56.792
Come check this out.

50:06.000 --> 50:07.417
You think he died in the crash?

50:08.458 --> 50:09.542
[Anant] He's been shot.

50:10.708 --> 50:12.917
Two to the body, one in the head.

50:20.917 --> 50:22.917
-[thuds]
-[creature chittering]

50:23.833 --> 50:24.958
[Anant breathing heavily]

50:25.042 --> 50:26.417
[Hoyt] Let's get the fuck out of here.

50:27.750 --> 50:29.875
-Yeah.
-Let's go.

50:35.042 --> 50:36.750
[metal clangs]

50:48.333 --> 50:49.750
[Morrow] Don't turn around.

50:53.833 --> 50:56.417
Slowly, weapons on the ground.

50:56.958 --> 51:00.792
Relax, friend,
we're Prodigy search and rescue.

51:01.917 --> 51:03.208
You've been in a crash.

51:03.292 --> 51:05.625
Just let me call the med team.

51:05.708 --> 51:07.542
-[gunshot]
-[Hoyt] Fuck. [breathing heavily]

51:07.625 --> 51:09.333
Don't make me say it again.

51:16.917 --> 51:19.042
[metal clinking]

51:19.125 --> 51:20.292
Side arms.

51:24.500 --> 51:25.500
Up.

51:27.250 --> 51:28.458
Back in the lab.

51:29.667 --> 51:30.667
Move.

51:45.000 --> 51:46.625
-[Anant breathing heavily]
-[Morrow] Stop.

51:47.667 --> 51:49.958
On the floor, back to the pipe.

51:50.042 --> 51:53.750
Dude, this building is gonna come down
any second.

51:58.042 --> 51:59.167
Cuff him to the pipe.

52:07.958 --> 52:09.458
[zip tie zipping]

52:10.583 --> 52:11.583
Now you.

52:16.542 --> 52:18.500
-[zip tie zipping]
-[grunts]

52:20.875 --> 52:24.542
-[metal clanks]
-Seriously. We won't even call it in.

52:25.375 --> 52:28.333
Just let us go and we'll pretend
this never happened, all right?

52:37.875 --> 52:38.875
[metal clanks]

52:40.417 --> 52:41.708
Where is Kavalier?

52:43.708 --> 52:45.583
The trillionaire?
How the fuck would I know?

52:51.333 --> 52:54.000
[Anant softly] Oh, shit.
Hey, he's a cyborg.

52:55.333 --> 52:58.500
Mother, lab specimens seem intact.

52:59.167 --> 53:00.792
Moving to track the fugitives.

53:04.875 --> 53:05.917
Brother, come on.

53:07.458 --> 53:08.833
You can't leave us like this.

53:09.833 --> 53:11.042
I'm not your brother.

53:11.125 --> 53:13.125
[♪ ominous music playing]

53:21.667 --> 53:24.417
[♪ dramatic music playing]

53:36.792 --> 53:37.792
[Siberian] Hey.

53:55.083 --> 53:58.083
-[static on radio]
-[Rashidi] Command, are you seeing this?

53:59.042 --> 54:00.792
We're inside the cryo-chamber.

54:01.625 --> 54:03.208
Looks like no survivors.

54:03.292 --> 54:05.917
[distorted radio chatter]

54:06.000 --> 54:07.000
[Rashidi] Command?

54:15.708 --> 54:17.083
-[Siberian] Hermit!
-[Hermit] I'm coming.

54:22.917 --> 54:23.917
[Siberian] What does that?

54:24.750 --> 54:25.792
[Hermit] I don't know.

54:32.083 --> 54:35.083
He's been dead a week, maybe more.

54:35.958 --> 54:37.708
You see the color of the blood?

54:37.792 --> 54:39.625
-[Siberian] Yeah.
-The coagulation.

54:41.917 --> 54:43.875
[Siberian] Wait, why did this ship crash?

54:44.583 --> 54:45.583
Hermit.

54:48.083 --> 54:49.625
[Rashidi] Something crawled out of here.

54:52.833 --> 54:53.833
[Siberian] What does that mean?

54:53.917 --> 54:55.292
[electricity crackles]

54:56.083 --> 54:57.792
[Hermit]
We gotta find what made that trail.

55:00.375 --> 55:02.375
[♪ eerie music playing]

55:18.583 --> 55:21.125
[Anant] Hey! We're in here!

55:23.792 --> 55:25.125
I think I can get my knife.

55:28.500 --> 55:31.875
Almost got it. [grunts, whimpers]

55:34.625 --> 55:36.125
-Jesus.
-[Anant] What?

55:36.208 --> 55:37.208
Something's on me.

55:37.292 --> 55:39.083
[Anant] What do you mean
something's on you?

55:39.833 --> 55:41.833
-I don't know. Fuck me.
-[Anant] Hoyt?

55:41.917 --> 55:43.250
Some kind of big-ass bug.

55:43.333 --> 55:44.833
-[Anant] What?
-[creature chitters]

55:45.667 --> 55:47.708
-[Hoyt grunting]
-[Anant] Fuck. Huh?

55:49.500 --> 55:52.375
-[groaning, breathing heavily]
-[Anant] Fuck. Fuck.

55:52.458 --> 55:54.167
Hoyt, come on, we need to stand up.

55:54.250 --> 55:55.417
I can't get it off!

55:55.500 --> 55:58.042
-Hoyt! We need to get up!
-Fuck!

56:03.542 --> 56:05.917
-Where's it gone? I can't see it.
-[Anant] Huh?

56:06.917 --> 56:07.917
[Hoyt screams]

56:08.000 --> 56:09.000
Hoyt!

56:09.083 --> 56:10.750
It fucking bit me!

56:10.833 --> 56:11.958
-Hoyt, stand up!
-[shrieking] Fuck!

56:12.042 --> 56:13.208
[groans]

56:16.708 --> 56:19.000
-Fuck! Hoyt!
-[groans]

56:19.083 --> 56:20.375
-[Hoyt breathing heavily]
-Hoyt.

56:22.375 --> 56:23.375
Hoyt.

56:24.500 --> 56:25.500
Hoyt!

56:27.833 --> 56:28.833
Hoyt.

56:29.917 --> 56:32.083
Fuck! [grunting, breathing heavily]

56:40.125 --> 56:41.375
[whimpers]

56:41.458 --> 56:42.958
[grunting]

56:43.875 --> 56:46.333
Oh, no. [grunting]

56:46.417 --> 56:49.875
No. No. Fuck. Fuck. No. [grunts]

56:50.792 --> 56:51.792
[screams]

57:07.542 --> 57:08.750
[indistinct radio chatter]

57:08.833 --> 57:09.833
[Slightly groans]

57:12.125 --> 57:14.458
[machine whirring]

57:34.167 --> 57:35.958
Used to be food, you know.

57:39.042 --> 57:40.417
[scoffs] Me?

57:43.125 --> 57:44.125
Humanity.

57:48.417 --> 57:51.458
Your lives were short
and filled with fear.

57:53.167 --> 57:55.250
Then your brains grew.

57:55.333 --> 57:58.250
You built tools and used them
to conquer nature.

57:58.333 --> 58:03.500
You built impossible machines
and went to space.

58:06.042 --> 58:07.708
You stopped being food.

58:09.708 --> 58:12.125
Or, I should say,

58:13.333 --> 58:17.667
you told yourself
you weren't food anymore.

58:21.833 --> 58:26.208
But, in the animal kingdom,
there is always someone bigger or smaller,

58:26.292 --> 58:28.833
who would eat you alive
if they had the chance.

58:28.917 --> 58:31.458
That's what it is to be an animal.

58:32.833 --> 58:37.250
You're born, you live, you die.

58:40.958 --> 58:42.708
[metal rattling]

58:46.000 --> 58:47.792
-[explosion]
-[groaning]

59:05.833 --> 59:07.875
My brother is not gonna die.

59:10.375 --> 59:12.125
Of course he will.

59:12.208 --> 59:13.208
[Siberian yelps]

59:13.958 --> 59:14.958
[Rashidi] Everyone okay?

59:15.625 --> 59:16.625
[Siberian] Yeah.

59:17.625 --> 59:18.625
Boss?

59:20.958 --> 59:22.333
We keep going.

59:22.417 --> 59:25.875
[Kirsh] Injury, illness, old age.

59:26.375 --> 59:27.458
They all do.

59:29.583 --> 59:31.708
Generation after generation.

59:33.833 --> 59:36.333
All we can do is watch and take names.

59:41.125 --> 59:42.458
No.

59:42.542 --> 59:44.750
[♪ "E5150" playing]

59:44.833 --> 59:46.333
He's not gonna die.

59:51.625 --> 59:52.625
I'm gonna save him.

01:00:09.458 --> 01:00:10.875
[♪ "The Mob Rules" playing]
